'use strict';
/* =====================================================================
   Concept Explorer: every concept in two formats built from ONE description.
   1. Diagram: a workflow diagram with proper shapes (cylinders for databases, pages for documents, funnels for models), swim lanes,
      labelled arrows and data packets that travel along them, and tiny particles drifting inside each block.
   2. Hologram: the same parts as lit 3-D glass shapes you rotate and zoom. Click a part to fly into it. Data moves INSIDE the parts:
      pistons slide in their cylinders and the crank turns, tokens stream through the tokenizer, attention arcs flash between tokens,
      a query point searches a vector database, signals pulse through neurons.
   The text of each part explains what it does and why. Algorithms (k-means, gradient descent, ...) live in 20_algos.js and use the same look.
   ===================================================================== */
